# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# City Government of Tanjay — front end
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. .env.local is git-ignored; this file is
# committed and must never hold a real secret. Nothing here can be one: Vite
# inlines every VITE_* variable into the bundle it ships, so anything written
# here is readable by anyone who opens the site. A key that must stay private
# belongs in the backend's own .env, behind the API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the API answers. No trailing slash — one is stripped anyway (see
# src/api.ts), but the canonical form is without.
#
# This is read at BUILD time, not at run time, because the output is a folder
# of static files with no server to ask. Changing it therefore means a
# redeploy, not a restart: on Vercel, set it under Settings → Environment
# Variables and then redeploy.
#
#   development   http://localhost:8000   (the default in src/api.ts, which is
#                                          the address `php artisan serve`
#                                          listens on, so a fresh clone runs
#                                          against a local backend unconfigured)
#   production    https://api.tanjay.gov.ph   — or wherever the Laravel app is
#                                               deployed. It must be https: a
#                                               page served over https cannot
#                                               fetch over http, and the
#                                               browser blocks it silently.
#
# Whatever is set here, the backend has to allow this site's origin back:
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS in the backend's .env, and
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_PATTERNS for Vercel's per-branch preview URLs, which
# change with every deployment. See backend/config/cors.php.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Build the demonstration instead: 1, or absent.
#
# Set it and nothing above is read. The site draws itself from the snapshot
# committed at public/demo/home.json, with the sample set's photographs and
# posters beside it under public/storage, and makes no request to any API —
# which is what lets the front end be deployed on its own, before the Laravel
# app has a public address.
#
# Regenerate the snapshot from a seeded local backend when the sample set
# changes (see the README, "A demonstration deploy"). It is a snapshot, so it
# is only as current as the day it was taken; a build that is meant to serve
# the city's real records must leave this unset.
#
# It is deliberately not a fallback for an API that fails to answer. See the
# note on DEMO in src/api.ts for why that would be the wrong thing.
VITE_DEMO=
